From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:32:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] macos: start CEF with the first CEF webview, not at launch

An app that bundles CEF started it in startEventLoop whenever the
framework was present: CefInitialize, then CefRunMessageLoop for the
life of the app. An app whose CEF webviews open later, or never, paid
for CEF's browser-process setup, its GPU and utility helper processes
and the mapped framework from the first second, and its launch waited
for CefInitialize.

The main thread now always runs [NSApp run], with ElectrobunNSApplication
(CefAppProtocol) when CEF is bundled. The first CEF webview starts CEF
on that run loop with external_message_pump: CEF asks for work through
OnScheduleMessagePumpWork and CefDoMessageLoopWork runs on the main
thread, immediately or from a timer in the common run loop modes and
never later than 1/30 s, after cefclient's
MainMessageLoopExternalPumpMac. CefShutdown runs at exit only if CEF
started. A failed start is final (CefInitialize runs once per process)
and the webview falls back to WKWebView, as it does without CEF.

The native wrapper no longer links the framework (-weak_framework): it
calls the C API through libcef_dll_wrapper's dylib stubs and loads the
framework with cef_load_library when CEF starts, as CEF's helpers
already do, so dyld does not map 300 MB of CEF into every launch.

The remote debugging port is still read when CEF starts, from
ELECTROBUN_CEF_REMOTE_DEBUGGING_PORT or chromiumFlags.
